    <h2 class="sp-section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="sp-faq">
        <div class="sp-faq-item"><h3>Can I use a foreign credit card to pay a Chinese hospital?</h3><p>Public hospitals generally do not accept foreign cards directly at the cashier. Use WeChat Pay or Alipay linked to your foreign card, or cash. Many international departments accept international cards — we confirm payment options before your visit.</p></div>
        <div class="sp-faq-item"><h3>How do I link my foreign card to WeChat Pay or Alipay?</h3><p>Go to Wallet/Pay settings in either app and add an international Visa, Mastercard, or JCB card. The app converts charges into your currency. Expect a small fee (around 3%) on larger transactions; hospitals accept these cards reliably.</p></div>
        <div class="sp-faq-item"><h3>Do Chinese hospitals take cash?</h3><p>Yes, in Chinese yuan. Withdraw RMB from bank ATMs or exchange at airport counters and banks. For large deposits, a linked payment app or bank transfer is more practical than large amounts of cash.</p></div>
        <div class="sp-faq-item"><h3>How does hospital billing work for international patients?</h3><p>Pay-as-you-go: a deposit at admission, charges as they accrue, and final settlement at discharge — with itemized invoices you can submit to your insurer.</p></div>
    </div>

